er a third.\n<Subject 3> is the scene, camera and light from <Picture 1> (场景与光感严格参考图1): a walk-in closet / dressing room seen as the REFLECTION IN A FULL-LENGTH DRESSING MIRROR with a vertical warm LED light strip along its right edge and a light frame, a round cream-white shaggy long-pile rug at center, light wood floor around it, a beige linen-texture back wall with hanging garments, a cream draped curtain on the right, a white storage hamper on the left. The view is a HANDHELD PHONE SELF-SHOT IN THE MIRROR (手持手机对镜自拍) with natural handheld wobble throughout. Lighting is AMPLE, BRIGHT and SOFT (充足明亮且柔和) — even, well-lit, airy warm-white light plus the mirror LED glow, no harsh shadows, clean and gentle. One continuous take, zero cuts.\n<Audio 1> is the VOICE-TIMBRE REFERENCE for the off-screen female narrator (S1): only the speaker's voice timbre, pitch and vocal texture are referenced — the original words, content, speaking pace, emotion and pauses in <Audio 1> are NOT copied or carried over; the target uses brand-new Chinese voiceover lines (about 50 Chinese characters total) delivered in this same voice timbre, in a natural relaxed sharing tone. The voiceover starts on the VERY FIRST FRAME and runs continuously, without any silent gap, all the way to the end of the video.\n\nTWO MOTION LOCKS (hold at every frame):\nLOCK A — SAME-SIDE NEAR PAIRING, FEET NEVER CROSS (外侧脚穿外侧鞋·内侧脚穿内侧鞋): the OUTER FOOT may ONLY enter the OUTER SHOE directly in front of it; the INNER FOOT may ONLY enter the INNER SHOE directly in front of it. Each foot travels STRAIGHT into its own nearest shoe — feet never cross, never swap sides, never reach across, and a shoe never ends up on the wrong foot. While a foot puts on its shoe, that shoe stays grounded and still (the foot moves to the shoe); it lifts only after the foot is fully inside. Total shoes always = 2; loose shoes on the rug go 2 → 1 → 0 one at a time, with the other foot and other shoe held still each step; no teleport, duplication or self-moving shoe.\nLOCK B — ONE CONTINUOUS ROTATION, NO ORIENTATION JUMP: when showcasing angles, every turn is a single smooth even rotation on small pivoting steps, visibly passing THROUGH every intermediate facing; the body never snaps or jumps between angles, and each view (front/side/back) is reached only by physically rotating through the angles between.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] A 10-second horizontal 16:9 one-take (zero cuts) sneaker seeding video, shot as a handheld phone mirror-selfie in the dressing room from <Picture 1>, bright ample soft light. The woman's lower body (black flared trousers, fair slender legs, pink-coral toenails) starts barefoot with the UNC blue-white sneakers from <Picture 2> in front of her feet on the cream shaggy rug. Under LOCK A she puts them on one at a time — outer foot straight into the outer shoe (rug 2→1, inner still), then inner foot straight into the inner shoe (rug 1→0), same-side, no crossing. She walks to the CENTER of the mirror frame and, under LOCK B, rotates smoothly and continuously to showcase the sneakers from different angles without jumps. A ~50-character off-screen Chinese voiceover begins on the first frame (0.00s) and runs continuously with no silent gap through to 10.00s, its voice timbre referenced only from <Audio 1> (new words, original content not copied). Handheld mirror-selfie wobble, one continuous take, bright soft even light. 10 seconds, 16:9.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> lower body from <Picture 1>: fully_preserved - exact fair skin, slender ankles/calves, pink-coral toenail polish, black flared long trousers; hips/thighs down only; outer foot→outer shoe and inner foot→inner shoe, feet never cross.\n<Subject 2> sneakers from <Picture 2>: fully_preserved - exact UNC blue-white color-block low-tops, perforated white toe, blue overlays/laces/collar, white mid-panel with blue swoosh, white midsole, blue outsole, yellow tongue label; exactly two shoes, loose count 2→1→0, no duplication/teleport, shoe stays grounded while foot enters.\n<Subject 3> scene/camera/light from <Picture 1>: fully_preserved - LED-strip full-length mirror reflection, round cream shaggy rug, light wood floor, beige linen wall with hanging clothes, cream curtain, white hamper; handheld phone mirror-selfie with natural wobble; ample bright soft even warm-white light with mirror LED glow, no harsh shadows.\n<Audio 1>: reference - only the narrator's voice timbre, pitch and vocal texture guide the new ~50-character Chinese voiceover; the original words, content, pace, emotion and pauses are not copied; the voiceover runs from the first frame continuously to the end.\nContinuity: fully_preserved - one unbroken take, zero cuts; angle changes are continuous rotations through every intermediate facing; voiceover is continuous across the whole timeline with no gap.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a 10-second horizontal 16:9 realistic sneaker seeding video seen entirely as the reflection in a full-length LED dressing mirror, shot as a HANDHELD PHONE mirror-selfie with natural subtle wobble throughout, authentic phone feel, one continuous take with zero cuts. The room is bathed in AMPLE, BRIGHT, SOFT even warm-white light plus the warm vertical LED glow along the mirror, no harsh shadows, airy and clean. The woman's lower body from <Subject 1> stands on the round cream-white shaggy rug at the left in black flared long trousers, fair slender ankles, pink-coral toenails, barefoot; the UNC blue-white low-top sneakers from <Subject 2> rest on the rug directly in front of her feet, separated into an outer shoe and an inner shoe aligned with her feet.\n[Shot 1] At 0.00s, ON THE VERY FIRST FRAME, the off-screen female narrator (S1) immediately begins in the exact voice timbre referenced from <Audio 1> (timbre only; new words, natural relaxed sharing tone, about 50 characters total) and KEEPS TALKING CONTINUOUSLY, with no silent gap, through every action until the video ends: <d>[Chinese] 姐妹们看这双上脚效果，蓝白配色干净清爽，正面显脚小，侧面线条流畅，鞋底很轻走路不累，搭裤子裙子都好看，特别百搭。</d> The opening frame shows both sneakers grounded and in clear view (2 loose, 0 worn) in front of her bare feet, mirror frame and LED strip visible, room bright and soft, the voice already present.\nFrom ~0.00s to ~1.50s she readies her stance, the flared trouser hems shifting slightly, both shoes still, the voiceover continuing.\nFrom ~1.50s to ~3.20s the OUTER FOOT travels STRAIGHT into the OUTER SHOE on its own side — no crossing — while that shoe stays grounded; the foot slides fully in, adjusts once naturally, and only then lifts the shoe worn on the outer foot, its spot now empty. The inner foot stays bare and still, the inner shoe stays grounded (1 worn + 1 loose = 2); narration continues over the action.\nFrom ~3.20s to ~4.50s the INNER FOOT travels STRAIGHT into the INNER SHOE on its own side — no crossing, no reaching across — the grounded shoe receives the foot, a small natural adjustment, then it lifts worn on the inner foot, its spot empty; now both sneakers are correctly paired (2 worn + 0 loose), rug clear of loose shoes, no teleport or duplication; narration continues.\nFrom ~4.50s to ~6.50s she walks forward to the CENTER of the mirror frame at a normal natural pace, blue-white sneakers stepping across the cream shaggy rug, flared hems swaying lightly, handheld wobble re-centering her in the mirror; the voiceover continues without pause.\nFrom ~6.50s to ~10.00s, centered, she showcases the sneakers from DIFFERENT ANGLES through ONE SMOOTH CONTINUOUS ROTATION on small pivoting steps: starting front (toe boxes, laces and side swooshes to the mirror, held a beat), rotating evenly through a three-quarter angle to a pure SIDE view held a beat (profile, midsole, outsole blocks), continuing through the other three-quarter angle to show the opposite side and heel, then rotating back to FRONT through every intermediate facing with no snap or jump, with an optional s